+\noindent \textbf{12.} A final execution-semantics verification, prompted by the question of whether Algorithm~1 ($\mathrm{LSTM}(x_t, h_{t-1})$, one step per update) matches the evaluation protocol (prefix-window recomputation; Section~4.1), showed that the two are \emph{not} equivalent under suppression: with the same frozen seed-42 checkpoints and calibrated thresholds, the evaluated recompute-on-update semantics gives $\mathrm{TTD}_{\mathrm{ef}} = 0.023$\,s at $44.7\%$ suppression (reproducing the published per-seed value exactly), whereas literal single-step skipping gives $0.170$\,s at $44.4\%$; under the fixed policy the two agree on FR and differ by $6$\,ms in $\mathrm{TTD}_b$. A new paragraph in Section~3.4 (after the complexity paragraph) states this distinction explicitly, assigns the published scheduled results and ms/frame measurements to the recompute-on-update semantics with per-frame compute $c_{\mathrm{gate}} + (1-s)\,W\,\mathcal{O}(\cdot)$, and marks the calibration and evaluation of the cheaper single-step variant as not performed; the latency-protocol sentence of Section~4.1 says the same at the point of measurement. The verification script and its per-variant CSV accompany the artifact. In the same pass: Figure~13 was split into two panels because its previous single axis mixed $\mathrm{ECE}_{\mathrm{cal}}$ (calibration family) with $\mathrm{ECE}_{\mathrm{pipe}}$ (reference configurations), two protocol-specific variants the paper itself declares non-comparable -- the accompanying text no longer claims jointly low ECE for AF-TOI on a shared axis (Section~4.8, Figure~13 paragraph and caption); the residual over-reaches on calibration were replaced by measured statements (``the temporal entropy profile around onset is unchanged'' in the measured trajectories; distinct operating points ``in the configurations measured here'', untested under shift); the Section~4.7 reading now states that the joint severity ordering spans two evaluation pipelines and is not a single-model measurement; the retrospective $m{=}3$ detection marker is now distinguished from causal confirmation ($(m{-}1)\Delta t \approx 0.21$\,s later) in Section~4.1; and the abstract-style phrases flagged in review (``epistemologically'', ``semantic grounding'', ``organizationally grounded'') were replaced by concrete statements, with Section~4.8 retitled ``Post-hoc Calibration Control''. A bug-scope trace confirmed that the stateless logger of item~11 fed only Table~13 and Figure~11: Figures~4--6 come from the GPU-regenerated prefix-window log whose skip rates match the replication campaign, Figures~7--10 from the per-seed evaluation CSVs, and the borderline macros produced by the old logger are defined but not used in the manuscript.
